        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8e5d33a9-2b8a-55bf-8993-e7977956686a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walt Disney, Esther Forbes, Hal Stalmaster, Elijah Isaacs\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, WED Enterprises\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, Anaheim, California, Wilkes County, North Carolina, Magic Kingdom, Disneyland Park\n- Works: Johnny Tremain\n- Topics: American Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Esther Forbes wrote the children's novel \"Johnny Tremain,\" which won the 1944 Newbery Medal.\n- In 1957, Walt Disney Productions released the film \"Johnny Tremain,\" based on Esther Forbes's novel and retelling the years in Boston, Massachusetts before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n- Hal Stalmaster, born March 29, 1940, is an American former actor known for the lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film \"Johnny Tremain.\"\n- Walt Disney initialized Magic Kingdom, and WED Enterprises designed it based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California, with a focus on fairy tales and Disney characters.\n- Elijah Isaacs (173?-1799) was an early farmer, statesman, and militia officer in Wilkes County, North Carolina during the American Revolution.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1b7136dd-a71d-5618-a3b6-0e918994f736",
        "text": "Page: Johnny Tremain (film). Sentence: Johnny Tremain is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions, based on the 1944 Newbery Medal-winning children's novel of the same name by Esther Forbes, retelling the story of the years in Boston, Massachusetts prior to the outbreak of the American Revolution.\nPage: Magic Kingdom. Sentence: Initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises, its layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California, and is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\nPage: Hal Stalmaster. Sentence: Harry Lapidus Stalmaster, known as Hal Stalmaster (born March 29, 1940), is an American former actor, known for his lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film of the American Revolution \"Johnny Tremain\", based on the 1943 Esther Forbes novel of the same name.\nPage: Elijah Isaacs. Sentence: Elijah Isaacs (173?\nPage: Elijah Isaacs. Sentence: -1799) was an early farmer, statesman, and militia officer in Wilkes County, North Carolina during the American Revolution.",
